  ('dbtrigger:public.agent_actions:trg_page_high_agent_action', 'database_trigger', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'trigger public.agent_actions:trg_page_high_agent_action', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W29', 'system.incident_opened', 'it_operations_engineer', 'system.task_engine', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'A high-severity agent action with no incident open for it yet is the declared start of W29 Incident and security response.', 'pg_trigger trg_page_high_agent_action on public.agent_actions -> fn_page_high_agent_action, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.company_goals:trg_goal_cascade', 'database_trigger', 'D RETIRE_OR_HISTORICAL', 'trigger public.company_goals:trg_goal_cascade', 'no business write measured (creates_work_now = false)', 'none — this class may not create business work', 'none', 'none', 'corporate_performance_director', 'system.task_engine', 'n/a — creates nothing to deduplicate', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'The org_tasks re-plan insert is disabled: it created operational work outside the kernel and no Phase B workflow starts from a goal retirement. Objective supersession and the legacy notice are kept. The owed behaviour is recorded in phase_b_phase_c_wiring_gap.', 'n/a', 'BUSINESS_SIDE_EFFECT_DISABLED_BEHAVIOUR_OWED', 'K31 RECLASSIFIED A -> D under §3 option B. It fires on old.active true -> new.active false — a goal being RETIRED, which is not a missed target; routing it to W02 would open a corrective-management run every time the founder tidies up a goal. No Phase B workflow starts from a goal retirement, so the task-creating statement is disabled, objective supersession and the legacy notice are kept, and the owed behaviour is recorded in phase_b_phase_c_wiring_gap.', 'pg_trigger trg_goal_cascade on public.company_goals -> trg_goal_cascade, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.inquiries:customer_abandon_ban', 'database_trigger', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'trigger public.inquiries:customer_abandon_ban', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W18', 'customer.support_signal', 'customer_success_director', 'system.task_engine', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'An abandonment is a new support signal about a customer, not a step inside an inquiry run.', 'pg_trigger customer_abandon_ban on public.inquiries -> trg_customer_abandon_ban, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.inquiries:trg_inquiry_received_a', 'database_trigger', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'trigger public.inquiries:trg_inquiry_received_a', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W05', 'customer.inquiry_submitted', 'rfq_qualification_manager', 'system.task_engine', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'The row that IS the new inquiry. Declared start of W05 Customer inquiry qualification; nothing exists to attach a signal to yet.', 'pg_trigger trg_inquiry_received_a on public.inquiries -> trg_inquiry_received, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.inquiry_matches:notify_matched_supplier', 'database_trigger', 'B EXISTING_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL', 'trigger public.inquiry_matches:notify_matched_supplier', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_signal_submit', 'W12 — the EXISTING run, never a new one', 'followup.due', 'supplier_matching_dispatch_operator', 'system.task_engine', 'signal: <source_type>:<source_id>:followup.due:<workflow_run_id>', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'A supplier being matched happens INSIDE the W12 run that approved the package. Starting a workflow per match would open one run per supplier for one inquiry.', 'pg_trigger notify_matched_supplier on public.inquiry_matches -> fn_notify_matched_supplier, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.notifications:trg_invite_status_on_send', 'database_trigger', 'B EXISTING_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL', 'trigger public.notifications:trg_invite_status_on_send', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_signal_submit', 'W09 — the EXISTING run, never a new one', 'provider.callback', 'supplier_onboarding_specialist', 'system.task_engine', 'signal: <source_type>:<source_id>:provider.callback:<workflow_run_id>', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'A status change on an invitation already sent. The registration itself is the class-A event; this is its delivery status.', 'pg_trigger trg_invite_status_on_send on public.notifications -> fn_invite_status_on_send, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.quote_items:quote_items_rescore', 'database_trigger', 'C READ_ONLY_MONITOR', 'trigger public.quote_items:quote_items_rescore', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'none — this class may not create business work', 'none', 'none', 'quote_evaluation', 'system.task_engine', 'n/a — creates nothing to deduplicate', 'TRACE-MONITORING', 'ACTIVE', 'No adapter. It recomputes a field on the quotes row its own item belongs to; dbtrigger:public.quote_items:quote_items_roll carries the revision signal for all three.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'RECLASSIFIED_INTERNAL_RECOMPUTATION', 'K22b RECLASSIFIED B -> C. All three quote_items triggers fire on every item change, and source_type is part of the idempotency key, so three emitters would deliver three signals for one revision instead of collapsing to one. This one is literally `update quotes set status = status`, a no-op touch whose only purpose is to fire the quotes triggers. quote_items_roll carries the revision signal for all three.', 'pg_trigger quote_items_rescore on public.quote_items -> trg_quote_items_rescore, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.quote_items:quote_items_roll', 'database_trigger', 'B EXISTING_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL', 'trigger public.quote_items:quote_items_roll', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_signal_submit', 'W14 — the EXISTING run, never a new one', 'supplier.quote_revision', 'quote_evaluation', 'system.task_engine', 'signal: <source_type>:<source_id>:supplier.quote_revision:<workflow_run_id>', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'Roll-up of item totals on a quotation that is already inside a W14 run. It fires on revision, not on first submission, so it is a signal on that run.', 'pg_trigger quote_items_roll on public.quote_items -> trg_quote_items_roll, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.quote_items:trg_items_submittable', 'database_trigger', 'C READ_ONLY_MONITOR', 'trigger public.quote_items:trg_items_submittable', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'none — this class may not create business work', 'none', 'none', 'quote_evaluation', 'system.task_engine', 'n/a — creates nothing to deduplicate', 'TRACE-MONITORING', 'ACTIVE', 'No adapter. It recomputes a field on the quotes row its own item belongs to; dbtrigger:public.quote_items:quote_items_roll carries the revision signal for all three.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'RECLASSIFIED_INTERNAL_RECOMPUTATION', 'K22b RECLASSIFIED B -> C. It recomputes and writes quotes.submittable on the row its own item belongs to — normalisation of one record, not the creation of business work. quote_items_roll carries the revision signal for all three quote_items triggers, so one edit to one line delivers one signal.', 'pg_trigger trg_items_submittable on public.quote_items -> fn_quote_recompute_submittable, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.quotes:trg_new_quote_sms', 'database_trigger', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'trigger public.quotes:trg_new_quote_sms', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W14', 'supplier.quotation_submitted', 'quote_evaluation', 'system.task_engine', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'The row that IS the new quotation. Declared start of W14. Its three sibling triggers on quote_items are class B because they fire on REVISIONS to that same quote — the distinction that stops one quotation opening four runs.', 'pg_trigger trg_new_quote_sms on public.quotes -> notify_new_quote_sms, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.supplier_dues:trg_due_paid', 'database_trigger', 'B EXISTING_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL', 'trigger public.supplier_dues:trg_due_paid', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_signal_submit', 'W16 — the EXISTING run, never a new one', 'provider.callback', 'payments_and_billing_manager', 'system.task_engine', 'signal: <source_type>:<source_id>:provider.callback:<workflow_run_id>', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'Payment against a due that already exists. The reveal payment that OPENS W16 is trg_reveal_receipt_a; this is settlement of an existing obligation.', 'pg_trigger trg_due_paid on public.supplier_dues -> qd_on_due_paid, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.transactions:trg_notify_refund', 'database_trigger', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'trigger public.transactions:trg_notify_refund', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W17', 'customer.refund_requested', 'trust_and_safety_manager', 'system.task_engine', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'A refund being requested is the declared start of W17 Refund and dispute handling; the resolution of that same refund is trg_refund_resolved and is class B.', 'pg_trigger trg_notify_refund on public.transactions -> qd_notify_refund_request, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.transactions:trg_refund_resolved', 'database_trigger', 'B EXISTING_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL', 'trigger public.transactions:trg_refund_resolved', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_signal_submit', 'W17 — the EXISTING run, never a new one', 'provider.callback', 'trust_and_safety_manager', 'system.task_engine', 'signal: <source_type>:<source_id>:provider.callback:<workflow_run_id>', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'Resolution of a refund already inside a W17 run. Routing it as new work would open a second W17 for the same transaction.', 'pg_trigger trg_refund_resolved on public.transactions -> qd_on_refund_resolved, enabled=t'),
  ('dbtrigger:public.transactions:trg_reveal_receipt_a', 'database_trigger', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'trigger public.transactions:trg_reveal_receipt_a', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W16', 'provider.payment_event', 'payments_and_billing_manager', 'system.task_engine', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over. The deployed trigger function calls fn_kernel_source_emit, verified against pg_proc at the time this row was written.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_COMPLETE', 'A reveal payment is the declared start of W16 Reveal and payment; settlement of an existing obligation is trg_due_paid and is class B.', 'pg_trigger trg_reveal_receipt_a on public.transactions -> trg_reveal_receipt, enabled=t'),
  ('edge:attach_photos', 'edge_function', 'C READ_ONLY_MONITOR', 'edge function attach_photos', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'none — this class may not create business work', 'none', 'none', 'document_intelligence_manager', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'n/a — creates nothing to deduplicate', 'TRACE-MONITORING', 'ACTIVE', 'No adapter. Measured against the deployed source: it writes NO table at all — it reads app_secrets and customers and returns.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'READ_ONLY_CONFIRMED_BY_MEASUREMENT', 'K30 RECLASSIFIED B -> C by measurement. It writes NO table at all: it reads app_secrets and customers and returns. An upload helper that changes no business state cannot be a signal about a run, and calling it one meant the register claimed a document arrival that never had a row behind it.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v7, verify_jwt=false with in-function Bearer -> auth.getUser -> 401.'),
  ('edge:claim_lookup', 'edge_function', 'C READ_ONLY_MONITOR', 'edge function claim_lookup', 'no business write measured (creates_work_now = false)', 'none — this class may not create business work', 'none', 'none', 'supplier_onboarding_specialist', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'n/a — creates nothing to deduplicate', 'TRACE-MONITORING', 'ACTIVE', 'confirm it writes no business work; raise a class-A request on threshold', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'READ_ONLY_CONFIRMED', 'Public "is this your company?" check, v4. It reads a lead by unguessable claim_token and returns; it starts nothing and changes no business state. Public by design — an invited supplier has no account yet, and v2 replaced the sequential id after v1 exposed the 20,470-row lead table.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v4. Public "is this your company?" claim check; v2 replaced the sequential leads.id with an unguessable claim_token after v1 exposed the 20,470-row lead database. Public BY DESIGN: an invited supplier has no account yet. | K17 2026-08-17: recorded_creates_work corrected true -> false. Deployed source writes only: agent_runs (own execution log). No workflow run, step run, task, hand'),
  ('edge:contact_submit', 'edge_function', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'edge function contact_submit', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W18', 'customer.support_signal', 'customer_success_director', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over by an AFTER INSERT trigger on the table it writes, so every writer of that table reaches the kernel and not only this function.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_VIA_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'First contact from the public website with no prior run. Declared start of W18 Customer issue and retention; a reply inside an existing conversation arrives through edge:messages_api instead.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v4, verify_jwt=true. Public contact form; honeypot spam guard; stores the message and emails the founder best-effort.'),
  ('edge:customer_api', 'edge_function', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'edge function customer_api', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W05', 'customer.inquiry_submitted', 'rfq_qualification_manager', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'No edit. It writes inquiries, quotes, quote_items or transactions, and those tables already reach the kernel through the triggers cut over in increments 1-3. A second emit here would deliver one business event twice.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'COVERED_BY_A_CUT_OVER_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'The customer portal submitting a new inquiry. Declared start of W05; documents and messages against an inquiry that already has a run are class B and go through the signal door.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v61. The customer portal API; called from src/components/me/** and src/components/portal/**. Creates and mutates inquiries.'),
  ('edge:customer_documents', 'edge_function', 'B EXISTING_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL', 'edge function customer_documents', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_signal_submit', 'W07 — the EXISTING run, never a new one', 'document.arrived_for_run', 'document_intelligence_manager', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'signal: <source_type>:<source_id>:document.arrived_for_run:<workflow_run_id>', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over by an AFTER INSERT trigger on the table it writes, so every writer of that table reaches the kernel and not only this function.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_VIA_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'Documents uploaded against an inquiry that already has a run. Attaching them is evidence on that run; opening a second W07 for a file added to live work is the duplicate this class exists to prevent.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v4. Customer document upload from src/components/portal/documents/api.ts.'),
  ('edge:inbound_email', 'edge_function', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'edge function inbound_email', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W05', 'supplier.registration_submitted', 'rfq_qualification_manager', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over by a trigger on the table it writes: inbound_messages, WHEN created_new_lead -> W09. The trigger reads the decision the function already made.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_VIA_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'K30 CORRECTED. K10 mapped this to customer.inquiry_submitted -> W05. It handles SUPPLIER correspondence: it matches or creates a leads row with business_role ''supplier'' and records the message. A supplier emailing in is not a customer inquiry, and routing it to W05 would open a customer-inquiry run for every supplier email the company receives. Cut over on inbound_messages where created_new_lead is true, so the trigger reads the decision the function already made.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v9. Inbound email classified into an inquiry; authenticates on x-webhook-secret.'),
  ('edge:inquiry_intake', 'edge_function', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'edge function inquiry_intake', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W05', 'customer.inquiry_submitted', 'rfq_qualification_manager', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'No edit. It writes a DRAFT in inquiry_intake; customer_api promotes a draft marked ready into public.inquiries and marks it consumed, and that insert already reaches the kernel through trg_inquiry_received_a. Emitting here too would open two W05 runs for one customer request.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'COVERED_BY_A_CUT_OVER_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'K30: COVERED, not wired. It creates a DRAFT in inquiry_intake, and customer_api promotes a draft marked ''ready'' into public.inquiries and sets the draft ''consumed''. That insert already reaches the kernel through trg_inquiry_received_a. Emitting here too would open two W05 runs for one customer request — and inquiry:{inquiry_id} cannot resolve from a draft, so every submission would have been refused anyway.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v22. Conversational intake: detects category, asks clarifying questions, emits a supplier-ready brief with a readiness score, persists drafts in inquiry_intake. The single most important unwired source in this inventory — it is where a customer inquiry begins.'),
  ('edge:messages_api', 'edge_function', 'B EXISTING_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL', 'edge function messages_api', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_signal_submit', 'W18 — the EXISTING run, never a new one', 'clarification.response', 'customer_success_director', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'signal: <source_type>:<source_id>:clarification.response:<workflow_run_id>', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'No edit. It writes inquiries, quotes, quote_items or transactions, and those tables already reach the kernel through the triggers cut over in increments 1-3. A second emit here would deliver one business event twice.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'COVERED_BY_A_CUT_OVER_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'Portal messaging. A message from a customer or supplier lands inside the run the conversation belongs to; the great majority are clarification answers, and none of them is a new inquiry.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v19. Customer/supplier messaging from src/components/portal/comms/api.ts.'),
  ('edge:pdpl_request', 'edge_function', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'edge function pdpl_request', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W28', 'customer.privacy_request', 'general_counsel', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over by an AFTER INSERT trigger on the table it writes, so every writer of that table reaches the kernel and not only this function.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_VIA_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'A privacy or data-subject request is the declared start of W28 Privacy, legal and compliance response. Consent withdrawal is edge:unsubscribe and is a different thing entirely.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v4, verify_jwt=false and NO authentication of any kind — required: UAE PDPL Art. 13-17 give a data subject a channel that does not need an account. K11 recorded its abuse capacity as a Phase D item; K10 records that the work it creates has no owner.'),
  ('edge:refund_flow', 'edge_function', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'edge function refund_flow', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W17', 'customer.refund_requested', 'trust_and_safety_manager', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'No edit. It writes inquiries, quotes, quote_items or transactions, and those tables already reach the kernel through the triggers cut over in increments 1-3. A second emit here would deliver one business event twice.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'COVERED_BY_A_CUT_OVER_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'A customer opening a refund with no dispute run yet. Declared start of W17 Refund and dispute handling.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v5, in-function Bearer -> getUser -> 401, then customers row -> 403 no_customer. Opens the refund case; the money movement itself stays behind the founder gate.'),
  ('edge:resend_inbound', 'edge_function', 'C READ_ONLY_MONITOR', 'edge function resend_inbound', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'none — this class may not create business work', 'none', 'none', 'document_intelligence_manager', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'n/a — creates nothing to deduplicate', 'TRACE-MONITORING', 'ACTIVE', 'No adapter. Measured against the deployed source: it books expenses from forwarded receipts and writes none of the eight tables K18 protects. It is not a bypass; it OWES a Phase B workflow, since W27 is a scheduled close and not a receipt arriving.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'READ_ONLY_CONFIRMED_BY_MEASUREMENT', 'K30 RECLASSIFIED B -> C, and it OWES a Phase B workflow. It books expenses from forwarded receipts — real business state, and no Phase B workflow declares it: W27 is a scheduled financial close, not a receipt arriving. It writes none of the eight tables K18 protects, so it is not a kernel bypass. Routing an expense receipt to W07 as a customer document, which is what the register said, would have been wrong.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v26. Inbound email with attachments, Svix signature verified. Receipts to finance, supplier documents stored and classified. A document arriving IS the W07 start event.'),
  ('edge:resend_webhook', 'edge_function', 'C READ_ONLY_MONITOR', 'edge function resend_webhook', 'no business write measured (creates_work_now = false)', 'none — this class may not create business work', 'none', 'none', 'lifecycle_channel_operations', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'n/a — creates nothing to deduplicate', 'TRACE-MONITORING', 'ACTIVE', 'confirm it writes no business work; raise a class-A request on threshold', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'READ_ONLY_CONFIRMED', 'Resend delivery events. A hard bounce writes email_suppressions — approved operational state, not business work. K10 recorded NO_WORKFLOW_IN_REGISTRY and it is right: W13 starts from an APPROVED QUEUED NOTIFICATION, not from its failure to deliver. When suppression crosses a threshold it must raise a separate class-A request, which is why this row is C and not simply exempt.', 'NO_WORKFLOW_IN_REGISTRY. Deployed ACTIVE v8. Resend delivery events, Svix signature verified (v4 security fix 19 Jul 2026 replaced a secret in the query string). A hard bounce writes email_suppressions. No phase_b_workflow starts from a delivery bounce: W13 starts from an APPROVED QUEUED NOTIFICATION, not from its failure. Handler owed to lifecycle_channel_operations. | K17 2026-08-17: recorded_cr'),
  ('edge:site_assistant', 'edge_function', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'edge function site_assistant', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W18', 'customer.support_signal', 'customer_success_director', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'Cut over by a trigger on the table it writes: assistant_logs, WHEN escalated -> W18. A question the FAQ answered is not a support signal.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'CUTOVER_VIA_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'The site assistant taking a first support signal from a visitor with no run. Declared start of W18 Customer issue and retention.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v19. The public chat widget (src/components/ChatWidget.tsx).'),
  ('edge:stripe_confirm', 'edge_function', 'B EXISTING_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL', 'edge function stripe_confirm', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_signal_submit', 'W16 — the EXISTING run, never a new one', 'provider.callback', 'payments_and_billing_manager', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'signal: <source_type>:<source_id>:provider.callback:<workflow_run_id>', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'No edit. It writes inquiries, quotes, quote_items or transactions, and those tables already reach the kernel through the triggers cut over in increments 1-3. A second emit here would deliver one business event twice.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'COVERED_BY_A_CUT_OVER_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'Confirmation of a checkout already in flight, so a run already exists. The webhook that OPENS W16 is edge:stripe_webhook; treating both as new work would open two runs for one payment.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v5. Browser-side payment confirmation callback; writes the reveal transaction and signs the file URLs.'),
  ('edge:stripe_webhook', 'edge_function', 'A NEW_WORK_REQUEST', 'edge function stripe_webhook', 'writes business work directly (measured live from the catalogue: creates_work_now = true)', 'fn_kernel_trigger_submit', 'W16', 'provider.payment_event', 'payments_and_billing_manager', 'system.webhook_receiver', 'trigger: <source_system>:<source_ref> (fn_kernel_trigger_submit default)', 'TRACE-SYSTEM-EXECUTION', 'ACTIVE', 'No edit. It writes inquiries, quotes, quote_items or transactions, and those tables already reach the kernel through the triggers cut over in increments 1-3. A second emit here would deliver one business event twice.', 're-point the handler at its pre-cutover write; the adapter row stays for the record', 'COVERED_BY_A_CUT_OVER_TABLE_TRIGGER', 'A payment event arriving from Stripe for an object with no run yet. Declared start of W16; the confirmation of a checkout already in flight is edge:stripe_confirm and is class B.', 'Deployed ACTIVE v13. Stripe provider webhook: verifies the HMAC signature with a 600-second replay tolerance, then writes transactions and logs every exit path to agent_runs. The one source in this inventory whose authenticity is cryptographically established before it is a signal at all.'),
